# patches/uboot/series — quilt-style ordered apply list.
# One filename per line (relative to this dir). '#' = comment, blank lines OK.
# Applied by scripts/apply-series.sh via `git am` (run from third_party/<uboot tree>).
#
# U-Boot RK3506 SoC support is ALREADY upstream (Jonas Karlman v2 merged into
# 2026.07-rc4), so this series holds ONLY the board/DT/defconfig delta. Verified
# 2026-06-15: applying this single patch to a clean 2026.07-rc4 (5ca1a73c) tree and
# rebuilding reproduces the booting U-Boot (binary differs from reference only in
# the embedded build-timestamp string — 29 bytes; binman-fake/ confirmed unneeded).

0001-rockchip-rk3506-add-AES-RK3506B-board-support-DT-def.patch
# SFC sampling delay-line tuning — same root fix as the linux side. Without this
# U-Boot cannot read the kernel FIT from NAND at 80 MHz (corrupt reads). Ports
# vendor rockchip_sfc_delay_lines_tuning() into the mainline U-Boot driver.
0002-spi-rockchip-sfc-add-delay-line-tuning.patch
# Raise SFC to 80 MHz + rockchip,max-dll=<0x17F>. Depends on 0002; mirror of the
# linux 0005 so U-Boot and Linux run the same tuned rate.
0003-arm-dts-rk3506-raise-SFC-to-80MHz.patch
